# [[ .Name ]] Helm chart

Chautari control plane for **[[ or .Estate.Org .Estate.Name ]]**, generated by
`chautari generate` from `estate.cdl`. Chart version and app version are both
`[[ .Version ]]`.

Each pod runs:

| Container | Role | Ports |
|---|---|---|
| `render-gateway` (init) | Renders the [[ .Dataplane ]] config from the CDL alone into the shared `/gateway` volume, so the data plane has a config at start | none |
| `chautari` | Checkpoint (`/v1`), admin API (`/api`), admin UI (`/`), MCP and A2A front doors. Rewrites `/gateway/[[ .GatewayConfigFile ]]` live as models, tools and keys change | 8080 |
| `gateway` | The [[ .Dataplane ]] data plane (`[[ .GatewayImage ]]`). Holds provider credentials; hot-reloads its config | 3000, 3100 (pod-local only) |

Only port 8080 has a Service, an Ingress and a NetworkPolicy opening. The data
plane is reachable from the `chautari` container over `127.0.0.1` and from
nothing else, so every request is authenticated, policy-checked, budgeted,
guarded and audited by the checkpoint.

## Install

From the generated output root (the directory holding `estate.cdl`):

```sh
helm install [[ .Name ]] ./helm/[[ .Name ]] \
  --namespace chautari --create-namespace \
  --set-file estate=estate.cdl \
  --set database.url='postgres://chautari:PASSWORD@db.example.internal:5432/chautari?sslmode=require'
```

The estate is passed with `--set-file` so the cluster runs exactly the file that
was reviewed. Changing it and running `helm upgrade` rolls the pods (the pod
template carries a checksum of the estate).

`helm install` prints how to reach the admin UI, read the admin token, mint an
API key and call `/v1/chat/completions`.

## Database

Postgres 14+ is required and is not bundled. Use a managed database (Amazon
RDS or Aurora PostgreSQL, Cloud SQL, Azure Database for PostgreSQL) or an
operator such as CloudNativePG, then either:

* set `database.url` (stored in the Secret this chart creates), or
* set `existingSecret` to a Secret you manage (External Secrets Operator,
  Sealed Secrets, the CSI driver) holding `CHAUTARI_DATABASE_URL`.

Use `sslmode=require` (or `verify-full`) against a managed database. Chautari
creates its schema on start. Every replica resyncs registry state from Postgres
every 15 seconds, so `replicaCount > 1` is safe; the default is 2 with a
PodDisruptionBudget of `minAvailable: 1`.

## Credentials

With `existingSecret` empty the chart creates a Secret holding:

| Key | Source |
|---|---|
| `CHAUTARI_DATABASE_URL` | `database.url` (required) |
| `CHAUTARI_ADMIN_TOKEN` | `secrets.adminToken`, generated when empty and kept across upgrades |
| `CHAUTARI_GATEWAY_KEY` | `secrets.gatewayKey`, generated when empty and kept across upgrades |
[[- range .ProviderEnvs ]]
| `[[ . ]]` | `providerKeys.[[ . ]]`, read only by the data plane container |
[[- end ]]

An `existingSecret` must use the same keys. Provider keys are optional there:
a missing key leaves the variable unset in the data plane.
[[- if .UsesBedrock ]]

## AWS Bedrock

This estate calls Bedrock (as a model provider or guardrail). The data plane
and checkpoint use the pod's AWS identity. On EKS, give the ServiceAccount an
IAM role allowing `bedrock:InvokeModel`,
`bedrock:InvokeModelWithResponseStream` and `bedrock:ApplyGuardrail`:

```yaml
serviceAccount:
  annotations:
    eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn: arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/[[ .Name ]]-bedrock
```

(or create an EKS Pod Identity association for the ServiceAccount). Set
`serviceAccount.automount: true` if your IRSA webhook requires the projected
token.
[[- end ]]

## Values

| Key | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `estate` | `""` | CDL source. Required; use `--set-file` |
| `dataplane` | `[[ .Dataplane ]]` | `agentgateway` or `litellm`; must match the estate |
| `replicaCount` | `2` | Control plane replicas |
| `image.repository` / `image.tag` | chautari image / appVersion | A repository with a tag or digest is used as-is |
| `gateway.image.repository` | `[[ .GatewayImage ]]` | Data plane image |
| `gateway.a2a` | `[[ .HasA2A ]]` | Route A2A through the gateway's :3100 listener |
| `existingSecret` | `""` | Use a Secret you manage instead of creating one |
| `database.url` | `""` | Postgres URL |
| `providerKeys` | one entry per provider credential | Provider API keys for the data plane |
| `policies` | `{}` | Extra `.rego` files mounted at `/etc/chautari/policy` |
| `otel.endpoint` | `""` | OTLP/HTTP endpoint (port 4318) |
| `aws.region` | `[[ if .UsesBedrock ]][[ with .Estate.Region ]][[ . ]][[ else ]]us-east-1[[ end ]][[ end ]]` | Region for Bedrock |
| `serviceAccount.annotations` | `{}` | e.g. IRSA role |
| `service.type` / `service.port` | `ClusterIP` / `8080` | |
| `ingress.*` | disabled | Standard Ingress (className, hosts, tls) |
| `networkPolicy.enabled` / `.from` | `true` / any | Ingress to :8080 only |
| `podDisruptionBudget.*` | enabled, `minAvailable: 1` | Applied when `replicaCount > 1` |

Pods run as UID 65532 with a read-only root filesystem, no capabilities and the
`RuntimeDefault` seccomp profile.
